meta {
  name: 1. Create DataSource (SQL)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasources
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "SQL Saga Geo Source",
    "description": "SQL (JDBC) pull source — geo sensor demo rows (lon/lat scalars)",
    "connectorType": "SQL",
    "configuration": {
      "driver": "postgres",
      "dsn": "postgres://postgres-sink:5432/geosink",
      "user": "geosink",
      "password": "geosink",
      "table": "saga_sql_input",
      "columns": ["*"]
    },
    "dataStructureVersionId": null,
    "assignments": []
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.body && res.body.id) {
    bru.setVar('sqlDataSourceId', res.body.id);
    // Versioned CORE URN of the stored connector config — the pipeline source node's `sourceRef`.
    // Re-captured after patch/release in case those re-version the config.
    if (res.body.configurationUrn) bru.setVar('sqlDataSourceConfigUrn', res.body.configurationUrn);
  }
}

tests {
  test("DataSource created", function() {
    const status = res.getStatus();
    // 201=created. This collection assumes a clean DB per run (CI uses an ephemeral stack); a 409
    // would mean a previous run leaked — fail loudly rather than carry a stale id downstream.
    expect(status).to.equal(201);
  });

  test("Has SQL connector type", function() {
    if (res.getStatus() === 201) {
      expect(res.body.connectorType).to.equal('SQL');
    }
  });
}

docs {
  **SQL saga step 1** — Prerequisites: create supporting resources before triggering the saga.

  Creates a **SQL (JDBC) pull datasource** ("SQL Saga Geo Source"). This is the one and only
  difference from the `dataset-saga-postgis` collection (which uses an MQTT source) — everything
  downstream (datastructures, dataset, POSTGIS sink, geoPoint pipeline) is identical, so any failure
  is attributable to the SQL **source** alone.

  The config mirrors the `datasources/contract` SQL shape (`driver`/`dsn`/`user`/`password`/`table`/
  `columns`), which the backend already accepts and round-trips at the API level.

  **Acceptance intent (TDD):** the pipeline engine cannot yet deploy a SQL source — the NiFi adapter
  throws `SQL source not yet supported` (`NifiFlowBuilder.sourceFragment`). This collection is the
  end-to-end **red** gate for that gap: it is expected to fail at the dataset-release deploy (step 9
  / verify step 10) until the SQL source is implemented, at which point it turns green. It mirrors the
  red unit test `NifiFlowBuilderTest.buildsSqlSourceChainCronScheduled`.

  **Expected Response:** 201 Created, body contains `id` and `connectorType: "SQL"`.

  **Post-condition:** Save `sqlDataSourceId` from `body.id`.

  **System Impact:**

  | Layer | Effect |
  |---|---|
  | Backend | DataSource record created in `portal_backend` DB with status `DRAFT` |
  | Config Adapter | — |
  | External System | — |
}
